{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_5e3af25f023e",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "The failure shows frame_len=3 when expected=1 at cycle 5. The current code never clears frame_len_next after frame_len_valid_reg pulses high. Patch 5e3af25f023e inserts `if (frame_len_valid_reg) frame_len_next = 0;` at line 81, forcing the counter to reset after a valid frame is reported so the next frame starts from zero rather than accumulating stale counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_1e51d2e21710",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "At cycle 5 the stimulus has tlast=1, tvalid=1, tready=1 while frame_reg is already 1. The outer condition (line 81) triggers, then the inner `else if (!frame_reg)` is skipped, so frame_len_next retains its previous value (2) and bit_cnt adds 1 → 3. Patch 1e51d2e21710 qualifies the outer guard with `&& (!frame_reg)`, preventing any length update on the final transfer of a frame and preserving the correct length (1) already captured on the first beat."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_3b8e3300b085",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 84,
      "mechanism": "Same root cause as patch_1e51d2e21710 but applied at the tlast branch (line 84). Adding `&& (!frame_reg)` to the `if (monitor_axis_tlast)` condition stops the final transfer from incrementing the counter again, so the frame length reported at cycle 5 remains 1 instead of growing to 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_158c82e15fb9",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 88,
      "mechanism": "Qualifies the new-frame initialization (`else if (!frame_reg)`) with `&& (!monitor_axis_tlast)`. This ensures that when tlast and tvalid coincide on the very first beat of a frame, the initialization path is taken instead of the tlast path, avoiding the double-count that produced frame_len=3."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_f178291ef6b5",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 88,
      "mechanism": "Changes the new-frame condition to `(!frame_reg) && (monitor_axis_tlast)`. For the failing trace this forces the single-beat frame to take the tlast branch (which sets frame_len_valid and clears frame_next) rather than the initialization branch, yielding the correct length of 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_14a0bc3c436d",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "Restricts the entire transfer-handling block to `monitor_axis_tlast` asserted cycles only. In the published trace the only valid+ready cycle with tlast=1 is cycle 5, so the block runs exactly once, adds bit_cnt=1, asserts frame_len_valid, and produces frame_len=1."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_a5fd054c48a1",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "Inverts the previous patch: processes transfers only when `!monitor_axis_tlast`. This would skip the final beat entirely, leaving frame_len at the value captured on the first beat (1) and still asserting frame_len_valid via the separate tlast check—if such a check existed; however the current tlast check lives inside the blocked region, so this patch risks dropping the valid pulse altogether."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The observed mismatch (frame_len=3 vs expected=1 at cycle 5) stems from the final transfer of a single-beat frame incrementing the counter a second time. The top-ranked patch (5e3af25f023e) directly clears the counter after a valid pulse, attacking the symptom. The next four patches (1e51d2e21710, 3b8e3300b085, 158c82e15fb9, f178291ef6b5) prevent the double-count by gating the update logic with frame_reg or tlast at the exact decision points (lines 81, 84, 88). Patches 14a0bc3c436d and a5fd054c48a1 take a coarser approach by filtering the entire block on tlast polarity; they happen to match the trace but are less robust for multi-beat frames. All citations reference the failing port frame_len and the line in the original source where each patch applies."
}
